COMMENT:
Received: 9/09/98 17:15
From: hvisser, hvisser@wxs.nl

Again a 'serious' piece for piano solo. It is build on the idea of
imbedding: {5, A B {3, A B {2, A B C D} C D} C D}.
You can get very rubato-rhythms at this way. The title is (until now)
'waves' (of the sea). It s a bit an 'impression', in the sense of a
reference to the music of Debussy.